  "articles": [
    {
      "sequence_id": 1,
      "text": "            In Unit 5, you encounter the verb form 'necesite', which illustrates the Spanish subjunctive mood. \nThe subjunctive is used to express wishes, doubts, necessity or hypothetical situations. \nThese forms often translate into English using phrases like 'that (you) may...', as in 'Necesito que venga' ('I need that she may come'). \nSubjunctive forms are not drilled in detail until later units, notably Unit 40, but recognising them early helps you identify when someone is expressing more than a straightforward fact. \nThe subjunctive mood is triggered by certain expressions of importance, doubt or desire, such as 'Es importante que...', 'No creo que...', or 'Quiero que...'.\n"
    }
  ],
